// Frozen fuzzexpr corpus for aot/run_fuzz.ql. DO NOT HAND-EDIT.
//
// Provenance: fuzzexpr.py (seed 1, --count 300 --depth 3) as of 2026-10-31,
// 300 gen_any trees followed by CHAIN_CASES (30 op pairs x 3) = 390 cases.
// expected = fuzzexpr.fmt(value) from the Python f64 oracle: IEEE + - * / and
// math.fmod, &&/|| return operands, == is type-strict, x/0 and x%0 (including
// an error operand) are ERR:DivisionByZero. Frozen once; no Python at test time.
//
// Counts: 384 value cases, 1 runtime error case (ERR:DivisionByZero), 5 cases
// rejected by the QLang frontend before codegen: a literal zero divisor is a
// static "division by zero" diagnostic (bootstrapped/parser.ql daCheckExpr).
// Those rows carry reject:"division by zero"; run_fuzz verifies both frontends
// reject them instead of dropping them. ge0274 is one of them: its zero divisor
// is on the never-evaluated || branch, but the diagnostic is not flow-sensitive.
//
// Oracle deviations, both explicit:
//  - ge0275: fmt() renders -0 as "0"; expected is "-0" (numeric contract and
//    std.Number.toString preserve signed zero). oracle:"0" records the raw fmt.
//  - runtime error cases keep the oracle kind in expected, while the top-level
//    diagnostic wraps it (e.g. TypeMismatch with a DivisionByZero cause);
//    run_fuzz requires the frozen kind anywhere in the stderr chain.
//
// Regeneration used a one-off /tmp script importing fuzzexpr; it is intentionally
// not kept in-repo. Regenerating requires fuzzexpr.py and the same seed/order.
let cases = [
